From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:44:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: enable the CPU cluster
 power gates

t8132.dtsi now leaves the CPU clusters' power-gate node disabled, for
a board that sleeps to enable, as the J713 does in its own file. The
J604 deep-sleeps and boots on a P core, and iBoot sets only the E
cluster's enable, so enable the node here. Without this the J604 would
lose the enables k881 gave it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index c88e1373d4..a5858080d6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -1707,3 +1707,11 @@ ramoops@10200000000 {
 		pmsg-size = <0x0>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Deep sleep needs both CPU clusters' power gates, and the J604 boots on a
+ * P core; iBoot enables E's only. t8132.dtsi leaves the node disabled.
+ */
+&cluster_pwrgate {
+	status = "okay";
+};
-- 
2.43.0

